xgboost's custom hatchling backend (packager/) drives CMake itself and
takes arguments only from its BuildConfiguration -- it reads no CMAKE_ARGS
-- and its python package loads libxgboost via ctypes from a plain-named
shared lib. Four mobile adjustments, all inert on desktop builds (they
activate only via FORGE_* env vars or on iOS/android platforms):

1. packager/nativelib.py: append FORGE_CMAKE_ARGS (recipe-provided
   toolchain/ABI/OpenMP args) after the backend's own CMake args, so ours
   win on conflicts.
2. packager/nativelib.py: _lib_name() switches on the BUILD HOST's
   platform, so a macOS-hosted Android/iOS cross-build would look for
   libxgboost.dylib while CMake produced libxgboost.so -- FORGE_LIB_NAME
   overrides it.
3. packager/nativelib.py: on any cmake failure the backend silently
   retries WITHOUT OpenMP -- a broken cross setup would "succeed" as a
   silently degraded build. With FORGE_CMAKE_ARGS set, re-raise instead.
4. cpp_src/CMakeLists.txt + xgboost/libpath.py: the lightgbm ctypes-on-iOS
   treatment -- on iOS name the lib .so (serious_python framework-izes
   *.so; loose dylibs miss the device/sim merge) and drop the
   VERSION/SOVERSION symlink chain (forge's wheel packer would dereference
   it into duplicate copies); teach libpath.py the ios and android
   sys.platform values (absent upstream -- flet iOS reports "ios",
   CPython 3.13+ Android reports "android") plus the .fwork pointer form.

diff -ruN xa/cpp_src/CMakeLists.txt xb/cpp_src/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/cpp_src/CMakeLists.txt	2020-02-02 01:00:00
+++ b/cpp_src/CMakeLists.txt	2026-07-08 00:41:09
@@ -399,6 +399,13 @@
   set_target_properties(xgboost PROPERTIES
     VERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION}
     SOVERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR})
+  if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
+    # mobile-forge: plain-named .so so the app packager's shared-object
+    # handling (framework-ization + signing) applies; no version symlinks.
+    set_target_properties(xgboost PROPERTIES SUFFIX ".so")
+    set_property(TARGET xgboost PROPERTY VERSION)
+    set_property(TARGET xgboost PROPERTY SOVERSION)
+  endif()
 endif()
 target_link_libraries(xgboost PRIVATE objxgboost)
 target_include_directories(xgboost
diff -ruN xa/packager/nativelib.py xb/packager/nativelib.py
--- a/packager/nativelib.py	2020-02-02 01:00:00
+++ b/packager/nativelib.py	2026-07-08 00:41:09
@@ -16,6 +16,11 @@
 
 def _lib_name() -> str:
     """Return platform dependent shared object name."""
+    # mobile-forge: when cross-compiling, the TARGET's lib name differs from
+    # the build host's convention (macOS host -> Android/iOS target, both .so).
+    forge_name = os.environ.get("FORGE_LIB_NAME")
+    if forge_name:
+        return forge_name
     if system() in ["Linux", "OS400"] or system().upper().endswith("BSD"):
         name = "libxgboost.so"
     elif system() == "Darwin":
@@ -52,6 +57,9 @@
             "-DKEEP_BUILD_ARTIFACTS_IN_BINARY_DIR=ON",
         ]
         cmake_cmd.extend(build_config.get_cmake_args())
+        # mobile-forge: cross-compile args from the recipe; appended last so
+        # they override the defaults above (e.g. -DUSE_OPENMP).
+        cmake_cmd.extend(os.environ.get("FORGE_CMAKE_ARGS", "").split())
 
         logger.info("CMake args: %s", str(cmake_cmd))
         subprocess.check_call(cmake_cmd, cwd=build_dir)
@@ -100,6 +108,10 @@
         try:
             _build(generator=generator)
         except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:
+            if os.environ.get("FORGE_CMAKE_ARGS"):
+                # mobile-forge: never mask a cross-compile failure with the
+                # no-OpenMP retry — surface the real error.
+                raise
             logger.info("Failed to build with OpenMP. Exception: %s", str(e))
             build_config.use_openmp = False
             _build(generator=generator)
